language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ contracting_costs: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ A contractor planning the construction of a house found that he would have to pay: $1,100 to the paper hanger and the painter; $1,700 to the painter and plumber; $1,100 to the plumber and electrician; $3,300 to the electrician and carpenter; $5,300 to the carpenter and mason; and $3,200 to the mason and painter. What does each man charge for his services, in dollars?
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/contracting_costs.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ paper_hanger: the charge of the paper hanger, in dollars
find paper_hanger : int(0..6000)
$ painter: the charge of the painter, in dollars
find painter : int(0..6000)
$ plumber: the charge of the plumber, in dollars
find plumber : int(0..6000)
$ electrician: the charge of the electrician, in dollars
find electrician : int(0..6000)
$ carpenter: the charge of the carpenter, in dollars
find carpenter : int(0..6000)
$ mason: the charge of the mason, in dollars
find mason : int(0..6000)

such that
$ the paper hanger and the painter together are paid $1,100
paper_hanger + painter = 1100,
$ the painter and the plumber together are paid $1,700
painter + plumber = 1700,
$ the plumber and the electrician together are paid $1,100
plumber + electrician = 1100,
$ the electrician and the carpenter together are paid $3,300
electrician + carpenter = 3300,
$ the carpenter and the mason together are paid $5,300
carpenter + mason = 5300,
$ the mason and the painter together are paid $3,200
mason + painter = 3200
